# __TITLE__ board

Board: __PROJECT_URL__
Linked repos: __REPOS__ (primary: __PRIMARY_REPO__)

All project, field, and option IDs are in [config.json](config.json). Do not rediscover them. Run every command through the shared CLI, which is also used by the GitHub Actions:

```
export LINEAR_BOARD_CONFIG=.agents/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/config.json
bash .github/linear-board/board.sh help
```

Run commands from the root of __PRIMARY_REPO__, with `LINEAR_BOARD_CONFIG` set as above. Below, `board` is short for `bash .github/linear-board/board.sh`. Refs look like `owner/repo#12`, `repo#12`, or `#12`. A bare number refers to the primary repo.

## Model

| Linear | Here |
|---|---|
| Workflow state | `Status`: Triage, Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Canceled |
| Priority | `Priority`: Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No priority |
| Estimate | `Estimate`: __ESTIMATES__ |
| Cycle | `Cycle` iteration, __CYCLE_DAYS__ days. Use `@current`, `@next`, `@last`, or a title such as "Cycle 3" |
| Project | Parent issue labeled `project`, with sub-issues. Lead = assignee. `Target date`, `Health` |
| Type | Label: bug, feature, improvement, chore |
| Duplicate | Closed as duplicate, Status = Canceled |

Automation that already runs, so do not repeat it by hand: a branch named `12-...` moves #12 to In Progress. An open PR moves it to In Review. A merge moves it to Done. Ended cycles roll over unfinished items. Backlog items get `stale` after __STALE_DAYS__ days. Urgent items get `sla-breach` after __SLA_HOURS__h with no activity. A weekly digest is posted as a project status update.

## 1. Triage inbox

1. Run `board triage`. It lists Triage items (oldest first) and items labeled `stale`.
2. For each item, read the issue (`gh issue view N -R repo`). Propose a type, priority, and estimate, then ask the user. Decide one item at a time unless the user wants a batch.
3. Apply the decision:
   - Accept: `board set REF priority=High estimate=3` and then `board accept REF Todo` (or `Backlog`, the default). Add the type label with `gh issue edit N -R repo --add-label bug` if it is missing.
   - Decline: `board decline REF "reason"`. This sets Canceled and closes the issue as not planned.
   - Duplicate: `board duplicate REF ORIGINAL_REF`.
   - A stale item that is still relevant: `board accept REF Backlog` (this removes `stale`). Otherwise, decline it.
4. End with a summary: how many accepted, declined, and marked duplicate.

## 2. Create an issue, Linear-style

Ask only for the values that are missing. Use the defaults: type from context, priority "No priority", no estimate, no cycle.

```
board create --repo REPO --title "..." --body "..." --type bug|feature|improvement|chore \
  --priority High --estimate 3 --cycle @current --due 2026-12-01 --parent '#4' --assignee @me
```

`--parent` makes the new issue a sub-issue of a project issue. Status defaults to Todo when a cycle is set, else Backlog. Use `--status Triage` to send the issue to the inbox. Report the URL.

## 3. Cycle planning and review

- Plan: `board plan --cycle @next` shows scope against the average velocity of the last 3 cycles (points completed), plus unscheduled Todo and Backlog candidates by priority. Propose a scope that fits capacity. After the user agrees, schedule each item: `board set REF cycle=@next`. If the cycle is over capacity, say which low-priority items to drop.
- Review: `board review --cycle @last` (or a title). It shows completed, canceled, still open, rolled over, and scope added after the cycle start. Summarize it in a few lines and point out patterns (for example, repeated rollovers or large unestimated items).
- List cycles: `board cycles`.

## 4. Projects and health

- Create: `board project-create --repo REPO --title "..." --lead LOGIN --target 2026-12-15 --health "On track"`.
- Add work: `board project-add PROJECT_REF CHILD_REF`, or create the child with `board create --parent`.
- Review: `board projects` shows the lead, target, health, and sub-issue progress.
- Update health: `board set PROJECT_REF health="At risk" target=2027-01-10`.
- Post a project status update (this shows on the board's status panel): `board status-update --status ON_TRACK|AT_RISK|OFF_TRACK|COMPLETE --body "..."`. Write the body from `projects`, `overdue`, and the current cycle. To get a draft of the automatic digest, run `board digest --dry-run`.

## 5. Overdue and SLA

Run `board overdue`. For each item, suggest an action: reschedule (`board set REF due=...`), raise the priority, reassign, or decline. Ask before you change anything.

## 6. Label sync

Run `board labels-sync`. It creates or updates the standard labels (types, `project`, `stale`, `sla-breach`, `rolled-over`) in every linked repo. To add a label everywhere, add it to `labels` in config.json and in `.github/linear-board.json` in each repo, then run the sync.

## Rules

- Ask before you close, decline, or bulk-edit issues.
- Use the CLI for writes. For something the CLI does not cover, use `gh api graphql` with the IDs from config.json.
- Item JSON for custom queries: `board items --status Todo | jq ...`.
